# The list, and everything derived from it. Real tasks about real, named people:
# probation reviews, salary conversations, contract dates, personal objectives.
# It is the private half of this repo and it never leaves the machine.
#
# One folder rather than a rule per file. It used to be four rules — todo.md,
# backups/, todo-backup-*.md, views.md — which meant anything new had to
# remember to add a fifth, and views.md nearly was that fifth. A folder cannot
# be forgotten. This is also what Obsidian opens as its vault, so the vault
# holds the list and nothing else.
#
# Inside it: todo.md, the board's backups and weekly snapshots, done-archive.md,
# views.md with the Dataview output, todo.md.tmp if a save ever crashes
# mid-write, and buckets/ — the bucket briefs and each bucket's own skills.
#
# buckets/ was a second rule at the root until 8 Sep 2026, when it moved inside
# the dataset. Its reasoning was always the same as this one's, and now so is
# its rule: a brief describes what he does in People or Design System, which
# names the people he does it with, and the skills beside a brief are Twinkl's
# process written down — probation forms, the interview question pool, the offer
# justifications. It moved because a brief is only true of one list; `twinkl`
# and `personal` have different buckets and different people.
#
# `BUCKETS.md` at the root is the tracked half: what a brief is for, how one is
# found, and the template to start from. The briefs themselves are his, and so
# is the README in each dataset's buckets/ saying which buckets that list has.
data/

# Obsidian's own state, wherever a vault is opened.
.obsidian/
.trash/

# Notes Obsidian creates by hand rather than from the list. Daily notes and
# canvases belong to whoever wrote them, not to this repo, and the vault sitting
# inside a git checkout is what makes this worth stating.
[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9].md
Untitled*.md
*.canvas

# Anything scratch, in case a working copy of the list is ever parked here.
*.local.md
scratch/

# macOS and Python noise
.DS_Store
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Dock launcher, rebuilt from kanban/icon.svg rather than committed.
To-Do Board.app/

# The menu bar companion's bundle, for the same reason: a plist, a shell script,
# a copied icon and a copied interpreter stub, all of it rebuilt in a second by
# companion/build-app.command. Keeping the recipe is worth more than keeping the
# build, and the stub is a signed binary that has no business in git.
To-Do Companion.app/

# Claude Code's own local state for this checkout: per-file agent symlinks and
# launch.json, which has carried paths under data/. All of it is specific to
# this machine, not to the project, so a clone should build its own rather than
# inherit ours.
.claude/
